"Internal Error ()\nciteturn1358view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://doi.org/10.4171/LEM/64-1/2-6\",\"lineno\":null}); \nURL https://doi.org/10.4171/LEM/64-1/2-6 is not accessible via this tool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[1904.04847v3] Units, zero-divisors and idempotents in rings graded by torsion-free groups (https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.04847v3)\nciteturn1358view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.04847v3\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Rings and Algebras\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 9 Apr 2019 (【5†v1】), last revised 20 Jul 2023 (this version, v3)]\nL9: # Title:Units, zero-divisors and idempotents in rings graded by torsion-free groups\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【6†Johan Öinert】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Units, zero-divisors and idempotents in rings graded by torsion-free groups, by Johan \\\"Oinert\nL14: \nL15: 【7†View PDF】 【8†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:The three famous problems concerning units, zero-divisors and idempotents in group rings of torsion-free groups, commonly attributed to I. Kaplansky, have been around for more than 60 years and still remain open in characteristic zero. In this article, we introduce the corresponding problems in the considerably more general context of arbitrary rings graded by torsion-free groups.\nL17: For natural reasons, we will restrict our attention to rings without non-trivial homogeneous zero-divisors with respect to the given grading. We provide a partial solution to the extended problems by solving them for rings graded by unique product groups. We also show that the extended problems exhibit the same (potential) hierarchy as the classical problems for group rings.\nL18: Furthermore, a ring which is graded by an arbitrary torsion-free group is shown to be indecomposable, and to have no non-trivial central zero-divisor and no non-homogeneous central unit. We also present generalizations of the classical group ring conjectures.\nL19: Comments:  | 17 pages. Changes from v2: Improved presentation and addition of recent papers to the list of references\nL20: Subjects:  | Rings and Algebras (math.RA)\nL21: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 16W50, 16S34, 16S35, 20F99, 16U40, 16U60, 16U70, 16U99\nL22: Cite as:  | 【9†arXiv:1904.04847】 [math.RA]\nL23:    | (or 【10†arXiv:1904.04847v3】 [math.RA] for this version)\nL24:    | 【11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1904.04847†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Johan Öinert [【12†view email】]\nL28: 【5†[v1]】 Tue, 9 Apr 2019 18:01:01 UTC (18 KB)\nL29: 【13†[v2]】 Thu, 2 May 2019 12:35:30 UTC (18 KB)\nL30: [v3] Thu, 20 Jul 2023 15:50:45 UTC (18 KB)\nL31: \nL32: Full-text links:\nL33: \nL34: ## Access Paper:\nL35: \nL36: View a PDF of the paper titled Units, zero-divisors and idempotents in rings graded by torsion-free groups, by Johan \\\"Oinert\nL37: \nL38:   * 【7†View PDF】\nL39:   * 【8†HTML (experimental)】\nL40:   * 【14†TeX Source】\nL41: \nL42: 【15†view license】\nL43: ### Current browse context:\nL44: \nL45: math.RA\nL46: \nL47: 【16†< prev】   |   【17†next >】\nL48: \nL49: 【18†new】 | 【19†recent】 | 【20†2019-04】\nL50: \nL51: Change to browse by:\nL52: \nL53: 【21†math】\nL54: \nL55: ### References & Citations\nL56: \nL57:   * 【22†SciX†scixplorer.org】\nL58:   * 【23†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL59:   * 【24†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL60: \nL61: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL62: \nL63: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL64: \nL65: [Button: ×]\nL66: \nL67: loading...\nL68: \nL69: Data provided by:\nL70: \nL71: ### Bookmark\nL72: \nL73: [